---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  active="About"
  description="Hi, I’m Chase, also known as code0100fun. I write Elixir, Zig, Rust, and C, and build things from web apps to hardware."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="orange-dash"></span> THE HUMAN BEHIND THE HANDLE
    </div>
    <h1>
      Hi, I’m Chase<span class="heading-dot">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>
      You might know me as{' '}
      <a
        class="text-link"
        style="display:inline;color:var(--orange);font:inherit"
        href="https://github.com/code0100fun"
      >
        code0100fun
      </a>
      . I write code and follow my curiosity from the browser all the way down
      to the hardware.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="about-layout">
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>Somewhere between software and silicon.</h2>
      <p>
        My projects span web apps, microcontrollers, video games, HDL hardware,
        game engines, a programming language, and an Erlang VM. Elixir, Zig,
        Rust, and C are my usual tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a place to write about those projects: the small discoveries,
        the implementation details, and the rabbit holes along the way. Expect
        plenty of source code and the occasional thing you can play with.
      </p>
      <h2>Build it. Understand it. Write it down.</h2>
      <p>
        A finished project is only part of the story. The interesting bits are
        often the choices made along the way, and what happens when an idea
        meets a real machine.
      </p>
      <div class="page-links">
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/code0100fun">
          <Icon name="github" size={17} />
          GitHub
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="https://x.com/code0100fun">
          <Icon name="x" size={15} />
          @code0100fun
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-stack">
      <h2>The usual suspects</h2>
      {[
        ['Elixir', 'Processes & the BEAM'],
        ['Zig', 'Systems & tooling'],
        ['Rust', 'Safety & performance'],
        ['C', 'Close to the metal'],
      ].map(([name, detail]) => (
        <div class="stack-row">
          <span>
            <i class={`dot ${name.toLowerCase()}`} />
            {name}
          </span>
          <span>{detail}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
      <div class="stack-row">
        <span>+ curiosity</span>
        <span>The common dependency</span>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
